Changes made to the original
----------------------------

As required by CC BY 4.0 section 3(a)(1)(B), the modifications are:

1. The corpus was restricted to the cleaned subset of 5515 requests used by

       Wenlong Ji, Lihua Lei, and Tijana Zrnic. Predictions as surrogates:
       revisiting surrogate outcomes in the age of AI. arXiv:2501.09731, 2025.

2. Two columns of AI-predicted politeness scores were added:
   `gpt_score` (GPT-4o-mini) and `predicted_score` (DeepSeek-V3.1).

3. Rows missing any of `gpt_score`, `predicted_score`, `Normalized Score`,
   `Feature_3`, or `Feature_10` are dropped at load time by `politeness.py`;
   the file itself retains all 5515 rows.

The comparative preference label used in the paper is not stored in the file.
It is derived at load time as V = 1{|W1 - Y| <= |W2 - Y|} (`politeness.py`).
